# taught_segment_role.p0t — INSEGNARE COME SI INTRODUCE UN INPUT, SENZA SCHEMA.
#
# M1 di apprendimento-assistito: una forma nuova viene ancorata a una forma che
# il teacher sa gia' usare. `segment_role/2`, il ruolo `prose_source` e la
# facolta' `reader` non compaiono nella lezione. Replay, transfer e ablazione
# avvengono nello stesso processo: e' crescita runtime, non una golden del binario.

[mock live]
!set PARROT0_BASE=kb/core/base.p0
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_WORLD_FACTS=1
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test a routed introducer is learned from a working model]
!timeout 60
# BASELINE: the wording has no typed route yet.
!mcp input.segment {"text":"study this passage: zibo has 2 gold."}
!expect! mcp "role":"prose_source"

# LESSON: no predicate, role, arity or faculty name.
> learn "study this passage:" as another way to introduce "read:"
< Got it - «study this passage:» now introduces the same kind of input as «read:».

# REPLAY: the exact red surface now reaches the existing reader.
> study this passage: zibo has 2 gold. nibo has 5 gold.
< Learned 2 fact(s), skipped 0.
> how many gold does zibo have?
< zibo has 2 gold.
> how many gold does nibo have?
< nibo has 5 gold.

# TRANSFER@3: new entities, predicates and rule shapes inherit the route.
> study this passage: fire causes smoke. rain causes puddles.
< Learned 2 fact(s), skipped 0.
> study this passage: tariq is a knight. every knight is a noble.
< Learned 2 fact(s), skipped 0.
> study this passage: the otter swims downstream. the otter swims often.
< Learned 0 fact(s), skipped 2.
# A scientific use of "error" must not be reclassified as compiler output:
# the explicitly routed role owns the whole payload by live KB policy.
!query faculty_dispatch(reader, eager)
!mcp input.segment {"text":"study this passage: an observational study is a design. measurement error causes uncertainty."}
!expect mcp "role":"prose_source"
!expect mcp "faculty":"reader"
> study this passage: an observational study is a design. measurement error causes uncertainty.
< Learned 2 fact(s), skipped 0.
!query causes(fire, smoke)
!query knight(tariq)

# ABLATION: removing only the taught evidence removes recognition immediately.
!forget segment_role(prose_source, "study this passage:")
!mcp input.segment {"text":"study this passage: vela has 7 silver."}
!expect! mcp "role":"prose_source"

# RETEACH in the same process restores it without rebuilding.
> learn "study this passage:" as another way to introduce "read:"
< Got it - «study this passage:» now introduces the same kind of input as «read:».
!mcp input.segment {"text":"study this passage: vela has 7 silver."}
!expect mcp "role":"prose_source"
!expect mcp "faculty":"reader"

[test routed faculty precedence is live knowledge]
!timeout 60
# With the precedence fact, even long explicit input is read, never continued
# as a story merely because `gen` is earlier in the registry.
> read: zora is a navigator. zora is a person. zora is calm. every navigator is a traveler.
< Learned 3 fact(s), skipped 1.

# Removing the arbitration fact exposes the old competing interpretation.
!forget faculty_dispatch(reader, eager)
> read: vega is a navigator. vega is a person. vega is calm. every navigator is a traveler.
<! Learned 4 fact(s), skipped 0.

# Restoring one KB fact restores route stability in the same binary.
!assert faculty_dispatch(reader, eager)
> read: mira is a navigator. mira is a person. mira is calm. every navigator is a traveler.
< Learned 3 fact(s), skipped 1.
